 # T-105 Triage output arrives as prose
 The triage agent sometimes returns a paragraph instead of the Triage JSON and output_key then raises. Make it reliable.
+
+## Evidence
+Status: implemented; offline checks pass; SDK-dependent tests written but **not run** (google-adk not installed). No live model call.
+
+- Cause: `triage_agent` combined `tools` with `output_schema`. On the API-key backend (README), ADK 2.8.0 does not send `response_schema` when tools are present; it adds a best-effort `set_model_response` tool. Prose then reaches `validate_schema`, which raises on save. The audit helper flagged `schema_with_tools_path_depends_on_backend` at agent.py:35.
+- Fix: `triage_agent` is now a `SequentialAgent` made of two agents. `triage_reader` uses tools and writes plain notes to `triage_notes`. `triage_formatter` has no tools and keeps `output_schema=Triage, output_key="triage"`, so the schema is enforced natively on every backend. `guard_triage` (after_model_callback) replaces invalid JSON, fenced JSON with surrounding prose, and provider errors (SAFETY etc.) with a valid `CANNOT_TRIAGE` record, so the save never raises.
+- Contract change: `Triage` gains `status: TRIAGED | CANNOT_TRIAGE`. `category` and `priority` are now nullable. Saved with `exclude_none`, so consumers must treat a missing key as None.
+- Offline (Python 3.9.13 + pydantic 2.11.2, not the project's 3.11): `pytest` → 11 passed, 1 skipped (tests/test_triage_agent.py, needs google.adk). check_response_schema.py: no unsupported keywords (info: 3 optional > 2 required).
+- Not run: tests/test_triage_agent.py (guard callback, scripted-model save path, request-capture of native schema). This also needs pytest-asyncio, which is not in the dependencies. No live check.
+- Retry budget inside the agent is 0: a callback cannot re-call the model. A genuine retry needs the Runner owner to re-invoke on `custom_metadata.contract_failure`; there is no such caller in this repo.
